## Context

Author ruling, 2026-11-07, after reading the climate-finance-het smelt report
(`memory/smelts/2026-11-07-retire-dream-consolidation.md`, PR #2022 there):
"smelt offers to promote harness rules. It should only nominate. Promotion
discussion is brood job later."

`skills/smelt/SKILL.md` § Native-note triage lane asks for a disposition
"**promote to rules**, naming the destination file and section". The run
above did exactly that: 8 rows, five pointing into harness rules
(`~/.agents/rules/workflow.md` § Autonomous action, § Delegation) or project
rules, each with a chosen section. Choosing a destination and section is the
start of a promotion argument, which belongs to brood (`skills/brood/SKILL.md`:
"scoped harness nominations, on explicit request"), not to a memory
consolidation pass. The author accepted the triage with "leave rules
promotion to brood"; the eight notes stay in the native store for brood.

## Change

In smelt's native-note triage lane, replace the "promote to rules" disposition
with a nomination for brood (say "nominate as a rule candidate"): a
one-line reason the note reads as a working rule, no destination file or
section, no wording. Brood takes the nominations as input and runs the
promotion discussion. Wording is the harness's call; keep "the author decides"
and "smelt writes no rule".

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Smelt's triage lane offers a rule *nomination*, without destination
  file, section or proposed wording.
- [ ] Brood's skill names smelt's nominations as an input to its promotion
  work.
- [ ] Smelt's statement that this lane is the single exception to "propose no
  rules" is updated to match (a nomination is not a rule proposal).
